  "notes": "Confessional topline pop across three documented sub-modes — Max Martin electropop, Antonoff synth-pop, Dessner folk-chamber — encoded as one straight-backbeat model rather than three. The research states the backbeat class plainly: \"backbeat on 2&4 straight\", so `session.halfTime` is false and the snare is `backbeat_24` against a parent genre that is half-time on 3, which is the largest single delta in this file. The chords come from the research's own words: \"diatonic four-chord loops, most characteristically I—vi(7)—IV—V\" with \"4- or 8-bar loops\", so that family carries top weight and the sevenths live in `extensions` rather than in the numerals. Drums follow \"programmed drum-machine claps and 4/4 backbeat\" plus a LinnDrum loop — a plain 8th hat, a low kick density, a `clap`-only stack and no trap roll vocabulary. The bass is \"electric/synth bass holding roots with minimal movement so the vocal owns the midrange\", which is `followRootsProb` 0.95 on a kick mirror, and there is deliberately no `bass808` block because the entry says \"no 808 idiom\" — inheriting the parent genre's explicit null is what gives this model a real bass part. Melody register is the documented \"mezzo-soprano writing sitting in the alto part of the range\" with verses \"sing-spoken in a narrow 3rd—5th band low in the register\" and choruses that \"jump a 5th—octave\", which is the `octaveJumpProb` and the interval spread. The countermelody is \"usually a stacked backing-vocal pad, not an instrument\", hence `sustain_pad` on top. Arrangement encodes the entry's \"explicitly load-bearing bridge\" and its cold-open. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are `bpm.mode` 84, the humanize pair and every drum probability: the research gives two tempo clusters (68—100 ballad/mid, 120—160 up-tempo) and no centre, so the mode is the midpoint of the stated core band and the outer band sets max. ⚠ The catalogue-wide BPM band carries the research's own [LOW-CONF] mark.",
